Z||000002||skitime||10-10-2001||07:38 PM||||I think you might have bad injectors.  Does the car start hard after it has been running or just when you first try to start it.  I wouldn't replace the wires just yet.  I think the wires often get replaced just because many people don't know how to do anything else.  I would try a good injector cleaner (Not the cheap stuff). If that doesn't help I have found the injectors need replaced if the car starts hard as if it was flooded the first time you start it but starts easier after that.  What is happening is some injectors leak fuel in the cylinders while shut off and when you try to start it it acts flooded till it blows out the extra gas.    <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
